\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {I.7}{\ignorespaces Photographies of different cloud types and phenomena. Cumulus congestus over Sorbonne University (Jussieu) (A). Kelvin-Helmholtz instabilities in cumulus clouds under asperitas clouds at sunset (B). Formation of a cumulonimbus at the end of the day above Paris Pantheon (C). Multilayered sky with nimbostratus on the left, precipitation in the background, cirrus far above everything else (D). Altocumulus field at sunset (E). Clear sky cumulus humilis crowned by Kelvin-Helmholtz instabilities (F). Big Kelvin-Helmholtz wave in stratocumulus over Scottish Highland mountains (G). Alto cumulus field in front of the full moon (H). All the pictures are from the author.}}{21}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
